---
import ContentPage from '../layouts/ContentPage.astro';
import Entry from '../components/Entry.astro';
---

<ContentPage title="Employment">
	<div class="entry-list">
		<Entry level={2} title="Full-Stack Engineer (Contract)" meta="Aug 2026 – Present" note="Client projects: details under NDA.">
			<h4>Professional credentialing and verification platform</h4>
			<ul>
				<li>
					Build and maintain the full stack of a national registry that verifies the credentials of professionals. The
					frontend is plain JavaScript and Vite; the backend runs on Node.js with Firebase Cloud Functions, Firestore and
					Cloud Storage.
				</li>
				<li>Built membership billing with Stripe, using webhooks to keep account status in sync with payments.</li>
				<li>
					Generate digital credential passes for Apple Wallet and Google Wallet, and built a public page where anyone can
					verify a member’s status.
				</li>
				<li>
					Connected third-party insurance-verification and background-check APIs. Members enter sensitive data on the
					provider’s own pages, so the platform never stores it.
				</li>
				<li>
					Built automated email and SMS reminders for expiring credentials, sent through scheduled functions at times suited
					to each member’s time zone.
				</li>
				<li>
					Set up CI/CD with GitHub Actions: unit, integration and Playwright end-to-end tests run against the Firebase
					Emulator Suite. Production monitoring uses Google Cloud alerts and uptime checks.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<h4>Multi-location medical wellness clinic</h4>
			<ul>
				<li>
					Redesigning the clinic’s website, which is moving off a no-code builder (Framer). The redesign went through four
					rounds of mockups, including a brand guide and a services hub.
				</li>
				<li>
					Built a 15-page static site in HTML and CSS: clean URLs, separate pages for each location with embedded maps, a
					membership page, and a searchable menu of 145 services.
				</li>
				<li>
					Planned and implemented technical SEO: a unique title and description on every page, canonical and Open Graph
					tags, structured data (JSON-LD) for the business, its locations and staff, its services and its FAQ, plus a sitemap
					and robots.txt.
				</li>
				<li>
					Wrote a map of permanent (301) redirects from the old site’s addresses, so the new site keeps the search rankings
					the old pages earned.
				</li>
				<li>Deploy preview builds with Cloudflare Workers.</li>
			</ul>
		</Entry>

		<Entry level={2} title="Merchandise Associate (part-time)" subtitle="The Home Depot" meta="Apr 2026 – Present">
			<ul>
				<li>
					Keep store inventory accurate by updating price labels, restocking shelves from overhead stock, and returning
					misplaced products to their correct locations.
				</li>
				<li>Find and handle damaged products to keep displays sellable.</li>
				<li>Help customers find products and connect them with the right staff for specialized needs.</li>
				<li>Set up seasonal displays.</li>
			</ul>
		</Entry>

		<Entry
			level={2}
			title="Computer Science Teaching Assistant"
			subtitle="Northern Illinois University · DeKalb, IL"
			meta="Aug 2025 – Dec 2025"
		>
			<ul>
				<li>
					Graded C and C++ programming assignments for CSCI 480: Principles of Operating Systems, and gave students written
					feedback on correctness and code quality.
				</li>
				<li>
					Answered students’ questions about operating-systems concepts such as processes, scheduling, memory management and
					concurrency.
				</li>
				<li>Worked 10–15 hours a week alongside PhD studies in computer science.</li>
			</ul>
		</Entry>

		<Entry
			level={2}
			title="Accounting Intern (part-time)"
			subtitle="ML Group Design + Development · Skokie, IL"
			meta="Jun 2022 – Aug 2022"
		>
			<ul>
				<li>Supported accounts payable and receivable by processing and recording invoices from companies and contractors.</li>
				<li>Tracked and reconciled company credit-card purchases using Microsoft Excel and the company’s ERP system.</li>
				<li>Worked with coworkers across different roles in a professional office environment.</li>
			</ul>
		</Entry>
	</div>
</ContentPage>
